				<Text>
					<Id>1585016279429</Id>
					<Name><![CDATA[text7]]></Name>
					<X>60</X><Y>300</Y>
					<Label><X>0</X><Y>-10</Y></Label>
					<PublicFlag>true</PublicFlag>
					<PresentationFlag>true</PresentationFlag>
					<ShowLabel>false</ShowLabel>
					<DrawMode>SHAPE_DRAW_2D</DrawMode>
					<EmbeddedIcon>false</EmbeddedIcon>
					<Z>0</Z>
					<Rotation>0.0</Rotation>
					<Color>-16777216</Color>
					<Text><![CDATA[The lime green represents 
susceptible cells in contact 
with infected cells, the dark 
green represent susceptible 
cells, and the red represents 
infected cells. The yellow 
outline shows the first cell 
infected in the foci, the foci 
origin. Infected cells are not 
allowed to proliferate and 
thus remain undivided. The 
white represents empty space, 
which healthy cells (limie 
green and dark green) may 
proliferate into. Healthy cells 
may also proliferate and 
subdivide into two, three, and 
four smaller cells.

Note: during the first 17 hours, 
infection of cells by free virus 
in the media is allowed. 
Thereafter cells can only be 
infected by cell-to-cell spread]]></Text>
					<Font>
						<Name>SansSerif</Name>
						<Size>14</Size>
						<Style>0</Style>
					</Font>
					<Alignment>LEFT</Alignment>
				</Text>
